        @(33,4,'Sweep half-angle','65 degrees or 22.5','The arc runs from the centre less this to the centre plus this; 0x10052370 builds the upper limit and 0x1005240F the lower','proven'),
        @(37,1,'At limit','0 in every captured copy, and 0x100525CA refuses anything outside 0 to 2','0 pins the angle at the limit and reverses the speed, 1 jumps to the far end of the arc, 2 stops there. Switched on at 0x10052397 and 0x10052432','proven'),
        @(38,4,'Turn-down speed','25 degrees a second or 20','Radians a second. Reaching the upper limit sets the signed speed to minus this, at 0x10052405; 0x1005258E forces it positive on arrival','proven'),
        @(42,4,'Turn-up speed','25 degrees a second or 20','Reaching the lower limit sets the signed speed to plus this, at 0x10052456, and it is what the signed speed falls back to when the wire carries a zero','proven'),
        @(46,4,'Sweep centre','234 degrees or 270.5','The direction the arc is centred on. The one field the client overrides: 0x1005251C tests it against zero and above it replaces the sent value with the direction the NPC is already facing','proven'),
        @(50,4,'Current angle','distinct in all 391 copies','Where in the arc the head is now. The sweep advances it by the signed speed times the frame time and turns it into the dynel heading','proven'),
        @(54,4,'Turn speed','plus or minus the two speeds above','Radians a second, signed - which way the head is going. Four values across the captures, two per NPC, one of each sign','proven'),
        @(58,4,'Unnamed','13 or 20','Read into the block at offset 0x20 and never read back. Two values from two NPCs will not separate a sight range from a level from a count. Checked on 2026-09-12 with the same sweep as the field at 29 - the receiver keeps the block at its + 0x24 and never reads the block''s + 0x20 from there','proven')
