        @('var',1,'Visible title','','','proven'),
        @('var','4 + count','Vehicle state','int count then that many bytes','The state of the vehicle that moves this character. 0x10067B62 reads the length, copies that many bytes out of the message stream into a BinaryStream at the message + 0xC4 and seeks past them, which is why nothing in the message reader parses them. The ribosome hands that stream to the character''s vehicle at 0x10078323 - n3Dynel_t + 0x50 is the Vehicle_t pointer, SetVehicle at N3.dll 0x10001107 - and slot 43 of every vehicle class is a reader: a Vector3 through 0x1000404E, then ten bytes widened into the movement state at vehicle + 0x178 by 0x10070981, then an int32, and then either four floats for a PlayerVehicle_t or an int16 count and that many floats for an NPCVehicle_t. That is 42 bytes for a player and 28 for an NPC with no floats - the two lengths the original CellAO server hardcoded, and its thirteenth byte, the one it fills with the movement mode, is the first of the ten','proven'),
