e export n3EngineClientAnarchy_t::N3Msg_GetPFName(unsigned int) at 0x10016AE6, so the first Identity is a playfield and "Unknown" is what the client prints when the table has no entry for it. The second is printed as a bare number beside it and nothing resolves it further. The int32 is settled by the arithmetic around it at 0x10043142: the client subtracts its own current time from it and divides the difference by 0xE10 and then by 0x3C to get the hours, minutes and seconds it prints, which makes it an absolute time rather than a duration. No capture contains one, so RaidCreatedCarriesNothingAfterTheKind and RaidLocksMatchesTheLayoutTakenFromTheClient pin the layout rather than checking it against retail; before this the message had no C# at all.'
