# The last inherited Trap/Mine identity is client-ignored compatibility
# metadata. Keep this resolution separate from the long forensic history above
# so the evidence remains readable and the generated status reflects the final
# result.
$known['TrapItemFullUpdate'].Evidence = 'A SimpleItemFullUpdate followed by a checked version, TrapDifficulty, two Identities and one flags byte. Extracted-client TrapItemFullUpdateIIR_t reader 0x100A28CA and writer 0x100A2954 agree byte for byte. Stat 289 names TrapDifficulty. Bit 1 is Armed: it gates CanBeTriggeredBy, disarming and the Feedback_MineIsArmed / Feedback_MineAlreadyDisarmed choice. Bit 0 is Revealed: it bypasses the perception-versus-TrapDifficulty roll after this character has spotted the trap. The first Identity is reserved client object metadata. Copy-back 0x100A29F4 stores it at TrapItem_t +0x1D4 and the outbound constructor preserves it, but construction initializes it to zero and no method in either concrete TrapItem_t or derived Mine_t consumes it. The apparent originator lead at 0x10086ABB was checked through RTTI and belongs to QuestBooth_t, not this hierarchy. The second Identity is a compatibility placeholder: the only sender zeroes it and neither copy-back nor any consumer reads it. No capture contains this message; TrapItemFullUpdateMatchesTheLayoutTakenFromTheClient pins the extracted layout.'
$known['MineFullUpdate'].Evidence = 'A fully identified TrapItemFullUpdate followed by a version and a reserved compatibility int32. Extracted-client MineFullUpdateIIR_t has reader 0x100A0DA4, writer 0x100A0DF1 and dispatcher 0x100A0EA5. The reader calls TrapItemFullUpdate''s reader for the inherited body, compares the appended version with static 0x101C2088, then preserves the int32 at message +0x8C; the writer emits the static and the same int32. The complete dispatcher only checks that the target exists, and inherited copy-backs do not consume the appended word. No capture contains one. MineFullUpdateIsATrapWithTwoMoreFields pins the extracted layout.'

